ginally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea?p=1122466#post1122466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except the Syndicate has the wealth of Pentex which means they control the entire Capitalist world. The NWO has been bleeding its influence into them for generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Pentex is being considered, are Kindred to be considered, too?<br /> <br /> How has the New World Order been bleeding influence into Pentex (is this the 'them' in your post?).<br /> Pentex is certainly not the 'entire capitalist world'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-29-2017, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T22:35:21-07:00","id":1122615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea?p=1122585#post1122585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Pentex is being considered, are Kindred to be considered, too?<br /> <br /> How has the New World Order been bleeding influence into Pentex (is this the 'them' in your post?).<br /> Pentex is certainly not the 'entire capitalist world'.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue would be very cut and dry. &quot;Pentex doesn't exit in Mage like The Union doesn't exist in Werewolf&quot; except unfortunately, or fortunately depending on your views, the whole Special Projects Division of the Syndicate IS canonically Pentex. It's not just a generic or new Nephandi faction but even in the Revised sourcebook, it's made clear Pentex has the backing of said division and exists in the Mage universe.<br /> <br /> Just like they killed one really huge ass vampire in India.<br /> <br /> Mind you, in Mage, I presume the SPD controls Pentex as well as being Nephandus and it's a huge ass Nephandus cult with trillions of dollars versus the Werewolf reality that Pentex is a Wyrm cult with some Wyrm worshiping Technomages inits employ.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T23:34:18-07:00","id":1122621,"title":"","content":"I've always thought there are two major faultlines in the Technocracy. First is the most obvious NWO vs Syndicate the position of money and goverment has always been sticky with both sides pushing their weight around so in the absense of feeling there's a common threat in the Traditions deciding to deal with this issue seems obvious.<br /> <br /> The other intrinsic fautline is Science vs Control. The major defections to the Traditions have been based on choosing Science over Control. And while there aren't any obvious Conventionwide groups like the two prototraditions before them the drive between &quot;We want to make the future now!&quot; and &quot;Guide and control the masses&quot; tears into the heart of the technocracy. Every convention has its conservative factions and every one of them has radical ideas that are crushed by the vast majority(with the possible exception of the IX who's Transhuman faction may have basically Won)<br /> <br /> There's also the obvious &quot;Nephandi corruption option&quot; but I find that kind of the most boring. I mean really That's just 1e Mage again except you have fewer choices on the sorts of magic you can use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T00:10:59-07:00","id":1122635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea?p=1122621#post1122621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other intrinsic fautline is Science vs Control. The major defections to the Traditions have been based on choosing Science over Control. And while there aren't any obvious Conventionwide groups like the two prototraditions before them the drive between &quot;We want to make the future now!&quot; and &quot;Guide and control the masses&quot; tears into the heart of the technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is the Ivory Tower, who are inclined to the 'Control' as you put it, due to, I'd say, the fact that they are practicing a 'soft' Inspired Science, which is (at least from some perspective(s) ) in contrast to the 'hard' Inspired Science of the Progenitors, Iteration-X and the Void Engineers. And the New World Order and especially the Ivory Tower are the ones who are the practical leadership of the Technocratic Union, as far as I'm aware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T01:19:30-07:00","id":1122650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea?p=1122635#post1122635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is the Ivory Tower, who are inclined to the 'Control' as you put it, due to, I'd say, the fact that they are practicing a 'soft' Inspired Science, which is (at least from some perspective(s) ) in contrast to the 'hard' Inspired Science of the Progenitors, Iteration-X and the Void Engineers. And the New World Order and especially the Ivory Tower are the ones who are the practical leadership of the Technocratic Union, as far as I'm aware of.</div> </div> </div> </div>The NWO and Syndicate definately lean more heavily towards the Control side and Ironically I'd say the post revised Void Engineers(while the prerevised VEs might have been the opposite) but that doesn't mean there aren't radical subfactions that want to take the paradigm in new and diffrent directions. I&quot;ll point out an example from the Syndicate book where the old guard is talking derisively about &quot;kids these days&quot; and their &quot;rep based economy ideas&quot;. There are all sorts of people drawn to the ideas of the Paradigm of resource management that the Syndicate espouses but they want to use hypereconomics to try something other than the capitalist machine. <br /> <br /> Look at the Progenitors, its not just about hard science their methodologies are all over the place, you have ones who just want to keep feeding people pills to move things along, ones who want to make humans better from gene tailoring on<br /> <br /> Three times. if we count the Union as the heirs of the Order of reason, they have fractured on this line. The first they destroyed their progressive Craftmasons, then when the Order reformed as the Union off went the Society of Ether. 50 years or so later with ww2 finished and the 50s dawning off fractures the Virtual adepts. Another Fracture point of radical vs control is coming but this time its not all wrapped up in one little Convention.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:18:55-07:00","id":1122770,"title":"","content":"...guys it was just a joke about the Emoji Movie being garbage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:26:49-07:00","id":1122772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OmegaZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea?p=1122770#post1122770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...guys it was just a joke about the Emoji Movie being garbage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the Union tearing itself apart has always been a cool idea.<br /> <br /> In my campaign, I just had the Technocracy collapse into a dozen competing factions.<br /> <br /> The Traditions did a double take as they hadn't been fighting them for a decade.<br /> <br /> It turned out the Traditions were all that were keeping it in place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T22:51:23-07:00","id":1122918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea?p=1122772#post1122772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my campaign, I just had the Technocracy collapse into a dozen competing factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you say more about the factions?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea?p=1122650#post1122650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at the Progenitors, its not just about hard science their methodologies are all over the place, you have ones who just want to keep feeding people pills to move things along, ones who want to make humans better from gene tailoring on</div> </div> </div> </div>Which of the Progenitor methodologies isn't 'hard' Inspired Science? They all seem to be so to me me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-31-2017, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T23:57:41-07:00","id":1122928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea?p=1122918#post1122918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you say more about the factions?<br /> <br /> <br /> Which of the Progenitor methodologies isn't 'hard' Inspired Science? They all seem to be so to me me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant its not about hard science vs soft. The Progenitors have some really solid breaks about the direction they should be taking(including &quot;we need to take over the Conventions for the Greater good!&quot;) but natural vs lab made, pharma vs genecrafting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T01:08:32-07:00","id":1122939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea?p=1122918#post1122918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you say more about the factions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> <b>The Throne</b>: An homage to the Seers of the Throne, the Throne is a faction of the Technocracy which has abandoned any and all pretense of being out for humanity and wish to use their powers to be as rich and powerful as possible. The Throne is allied with Pentex and the Camarilla's equivalent in my games and basically offer a very simple ultimatum to mages they encounter. &quot;Do you want be rich or dead?&quot; They may be allied with Threat: Null but primarily preserve Consensual Reality not to promote humanity but to make sure they're the only people with magick. The Throne actively works to slow down human progress and kill advancements that would lead to people awakening as they want to be the only people with that power. Their response to this treason to anything the Union stands for? &quot;Oh, grow up.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Thrones, notably, have added a NWO religion methodology which is effectively converted Celestial Choir, Akashic Brotherhood, and other Traditionalists who work to promote fundamentalist anti-science religious practices. It is a godless organization which truly offends many of its Traditionalist counterparts but wields great power in places the Union used to be quite weak.<br /> <br /> <b>The Nationalists</b>: Technocrats who have decided to infiltrate themselves into the governments of their home nations and work on a local level. The United States, Russian Federation, European Union, People's Republic of China, and so on are all separate factions now. This has also made them very very powerful within their spheres but they now work against each other. They've created several false organizations to work out of like Valkyrie, Majestic-12, Rainbow, and a newer bigger SAD.<br /> <br /> The Nationalists in America have accidentally clued way too many members of the establishment onto the supernatural and are presently scrambling to make up for that.<br /> <br /> <b>Invictus</b>: The reformer element of the Union has joined itself with the Sons of Courage to become basically Technocrat Monster Hunters. They've opted out of the Technocracy's Civil War (as this is generally called). Instead, Invictus works to hunt vampires, Revenants, Nephandi, and other creatures which go bump in the night. Invictus is growing because it's allied with Hunters and many Traditionalist mages have actually been willing to lend assistance. Invictus is probably more educated about supernaturals than most Technocrats now but is caught between the choice of whether to go after all reality-deviants or just the &quot;bad&quot; ones. There's more than cynicism at work there since they don't have the resources for the former.<br /> <br /> It has very high casualties but more or less equality between Acolytes and Enlightened Personnel.<br /> <br /> <b>The Foundation</b>: An alliance of Iteration X, Progenitors, Void Engineers, and Syndicate mages which have a much simpler goal than most. They exist for the purposes of advancing human science and technology, screw the whole reality war thing (which they are massively hypocritical on). The Syndicate mages here generally serve as marketeers while the bulk of the power is with the scientists and engineers. It's extremely rich and controls numerous former companies. Oddly, the Foundation does keep its own army and actively hates the Traditions. Generally, though, they prefer to fight the Ascension War with words and money. They are also at war as much with the Throne as anyone else.<br /> <br /> The Foundation has notably a loose alliance with the Virtual Adepts and has been working with them to try to &quot;convert&quot; the Sons of Ether into a group which would follow a coherent technocratic paradigm. There's been a big huge fight in the latter in my games anyway between the consistent scientists (essentially Technocrats allied to the Traditions who want a looser but not ridiculous paradigm) and the pseudo-science nutters.<br /> <br /> <b>Esoterrorists</b>: More of a catch-all term for Technocrats who have started flooding the markets of the supernatural world with Technocracy equipment. Part of this is ideological as they take a weird Reverse-Taftani approach to Consensual Reality as arming people with laser guns, robots, nanotechnology, and so on will improve the Union's paradigm as long as some of it work. They also protect themselves by leaving Paradox and the effects to fall on the people they sell them to. Other parts are for money or revenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-31-2017, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T08:32:49-07:00","id":1124311,"title":"","content":"I think you are missing one faction within these factions of the Technocracy Civil War:<br /> <br /> The Technocracy: This would be the remains of the Technocracy wishing to continue acting how Technocracy acted before the Civil War. One thing would change \u2013 (at first perhaps to somehow gain am edge despite their lessened number of Technocrats) the members of this faction would start becoming multi-Convention Technocrats \u2013 including belonging to more than two Conventions. Fully multi-Convention Amalgams and multi-Convention Methodologies would also be established.<br /> <br /> Most of the Ivory Tower \u2013 and much of the NWO...maybe \u2013 would stay in this faction \u2013 making other factions at least slightly paranoid whether this Civil War was from the start a plot \u2013 or a plan - of the New World Order of the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-28-2017, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T22:49:46-07:00","id":1126590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122213-technocracy-civil-war-campaign-idea?p=1122772#post1122772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my campaign, I just had the Technocracy collapse into a dozen competing factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to the Technocracy Civil War, I suggest that you take geography - including geography of countries, and the geography of specific cities - into account.<br /> <br /> Do you know if anywhere in the MtA books the number of Technocracy's Constructs is given, or suggested?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments"